  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 250 AM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nWarming trend back to well above normal temperatures next week:\n\nGlobal ensembles continue to be in good agreement on a slower \nwave progression of a digging trough/low over the SW CONUS. \nThis will lead to a prolonged amplified ridging pattern over our\narea, renewing southerly surface flow, keeping weather dry, and\ninitiating a warming trend to well above normal temperatures by\nthe middle of next week. Highs Monday are forecast to be around\n70 F, with highs reaching the lower to middle 80s by Wednesday \nthrough Friday. For context, normal highs for that time of year\nare in the upper 60s.\n\n\nMedium confidence in above normal temperatures to end October:\n\nAdditionally, the CPC has our entire region in a 60-70% chance \nfor above normal temperatures for the period of October 24-30. \nThis points to medium confidence that the synoptic pattern in \nplace will continue to favor above normal temperatures through \nthe rest of October.",
